        "subject": "LU-20076 tests: let replay-single 89 wait for statfs caches",
        "message": "LU-20076 tests: let replay-single 89 wait for statfs caches\n\nreplay-single test_89 compares OST free space before and after a\ndelete. The OST and the client each cache statfs for a second, so a\nreading taken within about 2 seconds of a ZFS commit can predate\nit. The ZFS sleeps in wait_delete_completed() used to hide this;\nnow that it forces a TXG commit instead, test_89 can read \"before\"\nwithout the data the previous test just flushed, or \"after\"\nwithout the freed object, and fails \"kbytesfree X > Y + margin\".\n\nOn ZFS, wait 2 seconds before the first reading. On all\nbackends, retry the final comparison for up to 10 seconds.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=replay-single fstype=zfs\nFixes: e5911ebb158d (\"LU-20076 tests: force a TXG instead of sleeping on ZFS\")\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Ifa42de07832936048a3a3aec60678103fd9c4d9b\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70738\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
